cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the McCluster adaptive-experience research software or methods, please cite this repository and the archived release DOI when available."
title: "McCluster Adaptive Experience Research Platform"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "McCluster"
    given-names: "Matthew"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-8988-8955"
abstract: >-
  A first-party research and production platform for adaptive digital
  experiences, music and creator discovery, recommender-system experimentation,
  Action Network participation, audience science, and commercial outcome
  measurement. The repository separates validated production policies from
  research policies and records opportunity sets, decisions, exposure,
  propensity, interaction and downstream outcomes for reproducible analysis.
repository-code: "https://github.com/mcclusterishere/mccluster"
url: "https://matthew.mccluster.org/research.html"
keywords:
  - recommender systems
  - adaptive user interfaces
  - human-computer interaction
  - audience analytics
  - music recommendation
  - contextual bandits
  - online experimentation
  - generative interfaces
  - creator economy
  - civic technology
